      "text": "Weathering is the chemical and physical breakdown of rocks at or near the Earth's surface. It is the first step in the geochemical cycle — releasing elements from minerals into solution, creating soil, and driving the long-term carbon cycle (silicate weathering = planetary thermostat)."
    },
